<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
2. Section 39.13 is amended by removing amendment 39&hyph;8659 (58 FR 44441, August 23, 1993) and by adding a new airworthiness
directive to read as follows:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=26 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=26 g=1 f=4 -->
Hamilton Standard: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=26 g=1 f=1 -->
Docket No. 94&hyph;ANE&hyph;26. Supersedes AD 93&hyph;16&hyph;02, Amendment 39&hyph;8659.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Hamilton Standard Models 14RF&hyph;9, 14RF&hyph;19, 14RF&hyph;21, and 14RF&hyph;23; 247F&hyph;1; 14SF&hyph;5,
14SF&hyph;7, 14SF&hyph;11, 14SFL11, 14SF&hyph;15, 14SF&hyph;17, 14SF&hyph;19, 14SF&hyph;23; and 6/5500/F
propellers installed on but not limited to Embraer EMB&hyph;120 and EMB&hyph;120RT; SAAB-SCANIA SF340B; Aerospatiale
ATR42&hyph;100, ATR42&hyph;300, ATR42&hyph;320, ATR72, ATR72&hyph;210; DeHavilland DHC&hyph;8&hyph;100
series, DHC&hyph;8&hyph;300; Construcciones Aeronauticas SA (CASA) CN&hyph;235 and CN&hyph;235&hyph;100;
Canadair CL215T and CL415; and British Aerospace ATP airplanes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Required as indicated, unless accomplished previously. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To prevent the inability to control the propeller blade angle due to tooth wear in the propeller control unit (PCU)
servo ballscrew internal spline (BIS) assembly, accomplish the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(a) Inspect the PCU servo BIS assembly for tooth wear in accordance with the Accomplishment Instructions of the following
Hamilton Standard Alert Service Bulletins (ASB), all dated April 7, 1994, as applicable: No. 14RF&hyph;9&hyph;61&hyph;A53,
Revision 5; No. 14RF&hyph;19&hyph;61&hyph;A25, Revision 4; No. 14RF&hyph;21&hyph;61&hyph;A38, Revision 4;
No. 247F&hyph;61&hyph;A3, Revision 3; No. 14SF&hyph;61&hyph;A59, Revision 4; and No. 6/5500/F&hyph;61&hyph;A11,
Revision 4; as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For a PCU with unknown time in service (TIS), and unknown TIS since the last inspection, on the effective date of
this airworthiness directive (AD), and that does not have a ballscrew quill damper installed, inspect within 200
hours TIS after the effective date of this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) For a PCU with 1,800 or more hours TIS or unknown TIS on the effective date of this AD, and either has not been inspected,
or has been inspected more than 500 hours prior to the effective date of this AD, in accordance with the applicable Hamilton
Standard ASB listed in paragraph (a) of this AD; and that does not have a ballscrew quill damper installed; inspect
within 200 hours TIS after the effective date of this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) For a PCU with 1,800 or more hours TIS or unknown TIS on the effective date of this AD, and that has been inspected within
the previous 500 hours TIS in accordance with the applicable Hamilton Standard ASB listed in paragraph (a) of this
AD, and that does not have a ballscrew quill damper installed, inspect within 500 hours TIS since the last inspection
in accordance with the applicable Hamilton Standard ASB listed in paragraph (a) of this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) For a PCU with less than 1,800 hours TIS on the effective date of this AD, and that does not have a ballscrew quill damper
installed, inspect prior to accumulating 1,800 hours TIS, or within 300 hours TIS after the effective date of this
AD, whichever occurs later. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) For a PCU that has a ballscrew quill damper installed in accordance with the following applicable Hamilton Standard
Service Bulletins (SB), or previous revisions: No. 14SF&hyph;61&hyph;67, Revision 1, dated May 6, 1994; No. 14RF&hyph;9&hyph;61&hyph;61,
dated December 9, 1993; No. 14RF&hyph;19&hyph;61&hyph;29, Revision 1, dated May 6, 1994; No. 14RF&hyph;21&hyph;61&hyph;48,
Revision 1, dated May 6, 1994; No. 247F&hyph;61&hyph;6, Revision 1, dated May 6, 1994; and No. 6/5500/F&hyph;61&hyph;19,
Revision 1, dated May 6, 1994; inspect within 1,500 hours TIS since installation of the ballscrew quill damper. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Thereafter, inspect at intervals described as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) For propellers that have a ballscrew quill damper installed in accordance with the applicable Hamilton Standard
SB listed in paragraph (a)(5) of this AD, or previous revisions, inspect at intervals not to exceed 1,500 hours TIS
since the last inspection required by this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) For propellers that do not have a ballscrew quill damper installed in accordance with the applicable Hamilton
Standard SB listed in paragraph (a)(5) of this AD, inspect at intervals not to exceed 500 hours TIS since the last inspection
required by this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) If PCU servo BIS teeth are worn beyond the limits specified in the Accomplishment Instructions of the applicable
ASB's listed in paragraph (a) of this AD, prior to further flight, replace the PCU with a serviceable assembly in accordance
with the Acccomplishment Instructions of the applicable ASB's listed in paragraph (a) of this AD, and thereafter
reinspect in accordance with paragraphs (a)(6) and (a)(7) of this AD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) Report the results of the initial and repetitive inspections required by paragraph (a) of this AD by utilizing
Appendix 1, ``Ballscrew Inspection Data,'' within 7 days of the inspection to the Manager, Boston Aircraft Certification
Office, Engine and Propeller Directorate, Aircraft Certification Service, FAA, 12 New England Executive Park,
Burlington, MA 01803&hyph;5299; Telex Number 949301 FAAANE BURL; fax (617) 238&hyph;7199. The reporting requirements
of this AD terminate on December 31, 1994. Information collection requirements contained in this regulation have
been approved by the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) under the provision of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1980
(44 U.S.C. 3501 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
) and have been assigned OMB Control Number 2120&hyph;0056. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

