<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Proposed Regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In consideration of the foregoing the Library of Congress proposes to promulgate a new part 705 of 36 CFR chapter 7,
reading as follows:. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->
PART 705_FINANCIAL ADMINISTRATION
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=20 g=1 f=1 -->
Sec.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=26 g=1 f=1 -->
705.1&blank;Salary offset.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Authority:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 5 U.S.C. and 5 CFR 550.1101.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;705.1 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Salary Offset 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Purpose.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 This part describes the rights of current and former staff members in the collection of debts owed to the Federal Government
by them and sets out the procedures for collecting debts through deductions from their pay following due process.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Debt
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is an amount owed to the U.S. Government from insured or guaranteed loans, fees, leases, rents, royalties, services,
sales of real or personal property, overpayments, penalties, damages, interest, fines and forfeitures (except
those arising under the Uniform Code of Military Justice), and all other similar sources.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) Disposable pay,
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 for purposes of this part, means that part of current basic pay, special pay, incentive pay, retirement pay, retainer
pay, or other authorized pay remaining after the deduction of any amount required by law to be withheld, such as Federal
taxes, retirement, court-ordered payments, and FICA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Staff member
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 refers to current and former employees who owe debts to the Library and/or other Federal Government agencies. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Procedures_
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Notification of indebtedness.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Director of Human Resources, or designee, shall notify the staff member, in writing, of the individual's indebtedness
to the Library and the intention of the Library to collect this debt by deductions from the individual's pay. This notice
shall be given not less than 30 days before any deduction is made. This notice shall state, at a minimum: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The Library's determination that a debt is owed, including the origin, nature, and amount of the debt; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The Library's intention to collect the debt by means of deduction from the staff member's disposable pay account;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The amount, frequency, proposed beginning date, and duration of the intended deductions; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) An explanation of the Library's policy concerning interest, penalties, and administrative costs, including
a statement that such assessments must be made unless excused; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The staff member's right to inspect and to copy Government records relating to the debt or, if he or she or his or her
representative cannot personally inspect the records, to request and receive a copy of such records; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) If not previously provided, the opportunity (under terms agreeable to the Library) to establish a schedule for
the voluntary repayment of the debt or to enter into a written agreement to establish a schedule for the repayment of
the debt in lieu of offset (the agreement must be in writing, signed by both the staff member and the Library, and documented
in the Library's files); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The staff member's right to a hearing conducted by an official arranged for or engaged by the Library (an administrative
law judge or, alternatively, a hearing official not under the control of the Librarian of Congress) if a petition is
filed as prescribed by the Library; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) The method and time period for petitioning for a hearing; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) That the timely filing of a petition for hearing will stay the commencement of collection proceedings; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(x) That a final decision on the hearing, if one is requested, will be issued at the earliest practicable date, but not
later than 60 days after the filing of the petition requesting the hearing unless the staff member requests and the
hearing official grants a delay in the proceedings; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xi) That any knowingly false or frivolous statements, representations, or evidence may subject the staff member
to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Disciplinary procedures appropriate under Library of Congress Regulation 2020&hyph;3, or any other applicable
regulations or statutes, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Penalties under the False Claim Act, section 3729 of Title 31, U.S. Code, or any other applicable statutory authority,
or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Criminal penalties under sections 286, 287, 1001, and 1002 of Title 18, U.S. Code, or any other applicable statutory
authority; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xii) Any other rights and remedies available to the staff member under statutes or regulations governing the program
for which the collection is being made; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
