<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 This proposed rule change is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
designed to adjust the PTO fees in accordance with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable provisions of title 35, United States Code, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section 10101 of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1990 (Public Law 101&hyph;508), as amended by the Patent and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Trademark Office Authorization Act of 1991 (Public Law 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
102&hyph;204). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Background 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Statutory Provisions:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Patent fees are authorized by 35 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
U.S.C. 41 and 35 U.S.C. 376. A fifty percent reduction in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the fees paid under 35 U.S.C. 41(a) and 41(b) by independent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inventors, small business concerns, and nonprofit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
organizations who meet prescribed definitions is required by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
35 U.S.C. 41(h). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Subsection 41(f) of title 35, United States Code, provides 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that fees established under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
35 U.S.C. 41(a) and (b) may be adjusted on October 1, 1992, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and every year thereafter, to reflect fluctuations in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Consumer Price Index (CPI) over the previous 12 months. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Section 10101 of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1990 (Pub. L. 101&hyph;508) provides that there shall be a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surcharge on all fees established under 35 U.S.C. 41(a) and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
41(b) to collect $107 million in fiscal year 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For fiscal year 1995, the PTO has proposed appropriation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
language that credits directly to the agency all patent fee 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surcharges collected pursuant to sections 10101(a) and (c) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
101&hyph;508). Under the proposal, the PTO will not request 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriations from fees deposited to the Fee Surcharge Fund 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as has been the practice from fiscal years 1991 through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Subsection 41(d) of title 35, United States Code, authorizes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Commissioner to establish fees for all other processing, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
services, or materials related to patents to recover the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
average cost of providing these services or materials, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
except for the fees for recording a document affecting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
title, for each photocopy, and for each black and white copy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of a patent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Section 376 of title 35, United States Code, authorizes the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Commissioner to set fees for patent applications filed under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Patent Cooperation Treaty (PCT). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Subsection 41(g) of title 35, United States Code, provides 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that new fee amounts established by the Commissioner under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Section 41 may take effect thirty days after notice in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and the Official Gazette of the Patent and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Trademark Office. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recovery Level Determinations:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The proposed rule would 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjust fees for a planned recovery of $571,439,000 in fiscal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
year 1995, as proposed in the Administration's budget 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
request to the Congress. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The patent statutory fees established by 35 U.S.C. 41(a) and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
41(b) are proposed to be adjusted on October 1, 1994, to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reflect any fluctuations occurring during the previous 12 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
months in the Consumer Price Index (CPI&hyph;U). In calculating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
these fluctuations, the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
has determined that the PTO should use CPI&hyph;U data as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by the Secretary of Labor. However, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Department of Labor does not make public the CPI&hyph;U until 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approximately 21 days after the end of the month being 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calculated. Therefore, the latest CPI&hyph;U information 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
available is for the month of April 1994. In accordance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
previously proposed rulemaking methodology, the PTO uses the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administration's projected CPI&hyph;U for the 12-month period 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ending September 30, 1994, which is 3.0 percent. Based on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this projection, patent statutory fees are proposed to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjusted by 3.0 percent. Before the final fee schedule is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
published, the fees may be slightly adjusted based on actual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
data available from the Department of Labor. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The proposed patent statutory fee amounts were rounded by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applying standard arithmetic rules so that the amounts 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rounded would be convenient to the user. Fees of $100 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
more were rounded to the nearest $10. Fees between $2 and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
$99 were rounded to an even number so that the comparable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
small entity fee would be a whole number. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Certain non-statutory patent processing fees established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under 35 U.S.C. 41(d) and PCT processing fees established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under 35 U.S.C. 376 are proposed to be adjusted up to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three percent fluctuation in the CPI in order to recover 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
their estimated average costs in 1995. Three patent service 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fees that are set by statute will not be adjusted. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three fees that are not being adjusted are assignment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recording fees, printed patent copy fees and photocopy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
charge fees. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
