<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
I. Background 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
A. Summary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under section 1886(d) of the Social Security Act (the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Act), a system of payment for the operating costs of acute 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital inpatient stays under Medicare Part A (Hospital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Insurance) based on prospectively-set rates was established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
effective with hospital cost reporting periods beginning on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or after October 1, 1983. Under this system, Medicare 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment for hospital inpatient operating costs is made at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
predetermined, specific rate for each hospital discharge. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
All discharges are classified according to a list of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
diagnosis-related groups (DRGs). The regulations governing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the hospital inpatient prospective payment system are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
located in 42 CFR part 412. On September 1, 1993, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
published a final rule with comment period (58 FR 46270) to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implement changes to the prospective payment system for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital operating costs beginning with Federal fiscal year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(FY) 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For cost reporting periods beginning before 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
October 1, 1991, hospital inpatient operating costs were the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
only costs covered under the prospective payment system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Payment for capital-related costs had been made on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable cost basis because, under sections 1886(a)(4) and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d)(1)(A) of the Act, those costs had been specifically 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
excluded from the definition of inpatient operating costs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
However, section 4006(b) of the Omnibus Budget 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100&hyph;203) revised 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section 1886(g)(1) of the Act to require that, for hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paid under the prospective payment system for operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
costs, capital-related costs would also be paid under a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prospective payment system effective with cost reporting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
periods beginning on or after October 1, 1991. As required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by section 1886(g) of the Act, we replaced the reasonable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cost-based payment methodology with a prospective payment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
methodology for hospital inpatient capital-related costs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Under the new methodology, effective for cost reporting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
periods beginning on or after October 1, 1991, a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
predetermined payment amount per discharge is made for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Medicare inpatient capital-related costs. (See subpart M of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
42 CFR part 412, and the August 30, 1991, final rule (56 FR 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
43358) for a complete discussion of the prospective payment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system for hospital inpatient capital-related costs.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
B. Major Contents of This Proposed Rule 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In this proposed rule, we are setting forth proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
changes to the Medicare hospital inpatient prospective 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment systems for both operating costs and capital-related 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
costs. This proposed rule would be effective for discharges 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
occurring on or after October 1, 1994. Following is a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
summary of the major changes that we are proposing to make: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
1. Changes to the DRG Classification and Relative Weights 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
As required by section 1886(d)(4)(C) of the Act, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
must adjust the DRG classifications and relative weights at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least annually. Our proposed changes for FY 1995 are set 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forth in section II of this preamble. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
2. Changes to the Hospital Wage Index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In section III of this preamble, we discuss revisions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the wage index and the annual update of the wage data. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Specific issues addressed in this section include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;FY 1995 wage index update. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Changes in the reporting of hospital wage index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
data. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Revisions to the wage index based on hospital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Impact of the revised hospital wage index. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Occupational mix adjustment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Research on refinements to labor market areas. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;State labor market options. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
3. Other Changes to the Prospective Payment System for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Inpatient Operating Costs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In section IV of this preamble, we discuss several 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provisions of the regulations in 42 CFR parts 412, 413, 485, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and 489 and set forth certain proposed changes concerning 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Definition of and payment for transfer cases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Review of DRG assignments. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;National average standardized amounts for FY 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Outliers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Rural referral centers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Determination of number of beds in determining the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indirect medical education adjustment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Disproportionate share adjustment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Changes affecting essential access community 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals (EACHs) and rural primary care hospitals (RPCHs). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Clarification of payments to rural referral 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
center/EACH hospitals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Direct graduate medical education payment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Other technical changes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
4. Changes and Clarifications to the Prospective Payment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
System for Capital-Related Costs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In section V of this preamble, we discuss several 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provisions of the regulations in 42 CFR parts 412 and 413 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and set forth certain proposed changes concerning the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Evaluation of provisions relating to obligated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital for hospitals subject to lengthy certificate-of-need 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(CON) process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
