<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940527-1-00049 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940527-1-00014 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=3 -->
Life insurance (if employee is owner or beneficiary) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accident insurance (if employee is owner or beneficiary) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Disability insurance (if employee is owner or beneficiary) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Long-term care insurance (if employee is owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
beneficiary) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Workmen's compensation insurance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Retiree health care cost (only current year, not the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extraordinary accrual required by FASB 106 (that is, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
non-cumulative portion)) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Taxes: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FICA_employers portion only 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Medicare taxes_employers portion only 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Unemployment insurance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
State or Federal unemployment taxes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Other: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Executive deferred compensation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Day care cost and allowances 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Tuition reimbursement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
b. Other Wage-Related Costs.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A hospital may be able to report an additional wage-related cost that does not appear on the core list if it 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meets the following criteria: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The wage-related cost is provided at a significant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
financial cost to the employer. To meet this test the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
individual wage-related cost must be greater than 1 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of total salaries after the direct excluded salaries are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
removed (Column 3, line 3 on Worksheet S&hyph;3, Part II). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Any wage-related cost that would be a fringe benefit if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reported to the IRS as a fringe benefit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The wage-related cost has not been furnished for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
convenience of the provider. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
We note that those wage-related costs that are required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to be reported to the IRS as salary (for example, loan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forgiveness and sick pay accruals) would not be included as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other wage-related costs, since the costs associated with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
these items are considered salaries and would already be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
included in the total salaries reported on line 1.01 of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Worksheet S&hyph;3, Part II. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
c. Wage-Related Costs (Excluded Area).
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Wage-related costs associated with employees in areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the hospital that are excluded from the data used to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calculate the wage index (such as a hospital-based SNF) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
should be removed from the total wage-related costs. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is not a new policy; however, to ensure that hospitals are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
removing these costs, we have added a new line on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Worksheet S&hyph;3, Part II. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In addition to the above changes, we are proposing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that, beginning on or after October 1, 1994, hospitals use 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
developing the wage-related costs contained in the Worksheet 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
S&hyph;3, Part II, for purposes of the hospital wage index. For 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all other purposes, however, Medicare principles will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
continue to apply in determining the allowability of fringe 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
benefit costs. The MTAG task force recommended application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of GAAP for purposes of developing wage-related costs used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to construct the hospital wage index. We believe it is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate to apply GAAP for these purposes because the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
function of the wage index is to measure 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
relative
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 hospital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
labor costs across areas. This function is distinct from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that of cost reimbursement, in which applicable Medicare 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
principles (which may differ from GAAP) measure the actual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
costs incurred by individual hospitals. We believe the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application of GAAP for purposes of compiling data on wage-related costs used to construct the wage index will more

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accurately reflect relative labor costs, because certain 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wage-related costs (such as pension costs) as recorded under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
GAAP tend to be more static from year to year. Application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Medicare principles, on the other hand, could create 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
large swings in these costs from year to year, particularly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in years when there are large over- or under-funded pension 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
estimates; such application might lead to a wage index that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
does not accurately reflect relative labor costs. Again, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emphasize that under this proposal, GAAP will apply 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
only
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of developing wage-related costs on Worksheet S&hyph;3 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Part II. Our policy requiring the use of applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Medicare principles for determining fringe benefits for all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other purposes remains unchanged. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The revised cost report and the HCFA&hyph;339 forms are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
currently being evaluated by the Office of Management and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Budget. Once these forms are approved, we propose to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implement the form to collect wage data for any cost report 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
beginning on or after October 1, 1994. However, we will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issue subsequent revisions to the forms and instructions to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reflect any changes incorporated in the final rule based on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
public comments. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
D. Revisions to the Wage Index Based on Hospital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Redesignation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under section 1886(d)(8)(B) of the Act, hospitals in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certain rural counties adjacent to one or more Metropolitan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Statistical Areas (MSAs) are considered to be located in one 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the adjacent MSAs if certain standards are met. Under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section 1886(d)(10) of the Act, the Medicare Geographic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Classification Review Board (MGCRB) considers applications 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by hospitals for geographic reclassification for purposes of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment under the prospective payment system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
