<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940527-1-00050 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940527-1-00014 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The methodology for determining the wage index values 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for redesignated hospitals is applied jointly to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals located in those rural counties that were deemed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
urban under section 1886(d)(8)(B) of the Act and those 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals that were reclassified as a result of the MGCRB 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decisions under section 1886(d)(10) of the Act. Section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1886(d)(8)(C) of the Act provides that the application of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the wage index to redesignated hospitals is dependent on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hypothetical impact that the wage data from these hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would have on the wage index value for the area to which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
they have been redesignated. Therefore, pursuant to section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1886(d)(8)(c) of the Act, the wage index values were 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by considering the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;If including the wage data for the redesignated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals reduces the MSA wage index value by 1 percentage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
point or less, the MSA wage index value determined exclusive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the wage data for the redesignated hospitals applies to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the redesignated hospitals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;If including the wage data for the redesignated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals reduces the wage index value for the area to which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the hospitals are redesignated by more than 1 percentage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
point, the hospitals that are redesignated are subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the wage index value of the area that results from including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the wage data of the redesignated hospitals (the ``combined'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wage index value). However, the wage index value for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignated hospitals cannot be reduced below the wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
index value for the rural areas of the State in which the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals are located. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Rural areas whose wage index values would be reduced by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
excluding the data for hospitals that have been redesignated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to another area continue to have their wage index calculated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as if no redesignation had occurred. Those rural areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whose wage index value increases as a result of excluding 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the wage data for the hospitals that have been redesignated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to another area have their wage index calculated exclusive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the redesignated hospitals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The wage index value for an urban area is calculated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exclusive of the wage data for hospitals that have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclassified to another area. However, geographic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclassification may not reduce the wage index for an urban 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area below the Statewide rural average, provided the wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
index prior to reclassification was greater than the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Statewide rural wage index value. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Section 13501(b) of Public Law 103&hyph;66 amended section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1886(d)(8)(C) of the Act to provide that a change in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
classification of hospitals from one area to another may not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
result in the reduction in the wage index for any urban area 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whose wage index is below the rural wage index for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
State. This provision also applies to any urban area that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
encompasses an entire State. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
We note that, except for those rural areas where 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignation would reduce the rural wage index value, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the situation described above that was addressed by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section 13501(b) of Public Law 103&hyph;66, the wage index value 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for each area is computed exclusive of the data for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals that have been redesignated from the area for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of their wage index. As a result, several MSAs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
listed in Table 4a have no hospitals remaining in the MSA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
This is because all the hospitals originally in these MSAs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have been reclassified to another area by the MGCRB. For 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
those areas, we have listed the Statewide rural wage index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
value. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The proposed revised wage index values effective for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
discharges occurring on or after October 1, 1994 are shown 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in Tables 4a, 4b, and 4c of the addendum to this proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule. Hospitals that are redesignated should use the wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
index values shown in Table 4c. For some areas, more than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
one wage index value will be shown in Table 4c. This occurs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
when hospitals from more than one State are included in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
group of redesignated hospitals, and one State has a higher 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Statewide rural wage index value than the wage index value 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
otherwise applicable to the redesignated hospitals. Tables 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
4d and 4e list the average hourly wage for each labor market 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area based on the FY 1991 wage data. In addition, we have 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
expanded Table 3c (Hospital Case-Mix Indexes for Discharges) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to include the average hourly wage for each hospital based 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on the FY 1991 data. The average hourly wage published in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the final rule will be used by the MGCRB to evaluate if a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital meets the reclassification criteria. Hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that choose to apply before publication of the final rule 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
can use the proposed wage data in applying to the MGCRB for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wage index reclassifications that would be effective for FY 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1996. We note that in adjudicating these wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclassification requests during FY 1995, the MGCRB will use 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the average hourly wages for each hospital and labor market 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area that are reflected in the final FY 1995 wage index. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The proposed FY 1995 wage index values incorporate all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclassification decisions made by the MGCRB for FY 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
At the time this proposed wage index was constructed, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
MGCRB had completed its review. There were 429 hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignated for purposes of the wage index (including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospitals redesignated under both sections 1886(d)(8)(B) and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1886(d)(10) of the Act). This number does not include MGCRB 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decisions that are still under review by the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Any changes to the wage index that result from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
withdrawals of requests for reclassification, wage index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
corrections, appeals, and the Administrator's review process 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will be incorporated into the wage index values published in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the final rule. The changes may affect not only the wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
index value for specific geographic areas, but also whether 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignated hospitals receive the wage index value for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area to which they are redesignated or a combined wage index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that includes the data for both the hospitals already in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area and the redesignated hospitals. Further, the wage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
index value for the area from which the hospitals are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redesignated may be affected. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Under &sect;412.273, hospitals that have been reclassified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the MGCRB are permitted to withdraw their applications 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within 45 days of the publication of this 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
document. The request for withdrawal of an application for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclassification that would be effective in FY 1995 must be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
received by the MGCRB by [OFR: Insert date 45 days after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
date of publication]. A hospital that requests to withdraw 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its application may not request that the MGCRB decision be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reinstated after publication of the final wage index values. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



