<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
2. Discharges 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 412.96(c)(2)(i) provides that HCFA will set 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forth the national and regional numbers of discharges in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each year's annual notice of prospective payment rates for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of determining referral center status. As 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in section 1886(d)(5)(C)(ii) of the Act, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
national standard is set at 5,000 discharges. However, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are proposing to update the regional standards. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposed regional standards are based on discharges for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
urban hospitals' cost reporting periods that began during 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1992 (that is, October 1, 1991 through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
September 30, 1992). That is the latest year for which we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have complete discharge data available. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Therefore, in addition to meeting other criteria, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are proposing that to qualify for initial rural referral 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
center status for cost reporting periods beginning on or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after October 1, 1994, the number of discharges a hospital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
must have for its cost reporting period that began during 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1993 would have to be at least_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;5,000; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

