<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Its average age of fixed assets is at or above the 75th percentile for the hospital's first cost reporting period
beginning on or after October 1, 1991; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Its average age of fixed assets in a subsequent cost reporting period (but no later than the last cost reporting
period beginning before October 1, 2001) declines by at least 50 percent from its average age of fixed assets in the
first cost reporting period beginning on or after October 1, 1991. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Planning authority approval. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The hospital must obtain any required approval from a State or local planning authority. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Excess capacity test for urban hospitals. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Urban hospitals that are not required to receive approval from a State or local planning authority must demonstrate
that either_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The overall average occupancy rate in its metropolitan statistical area is at least 80 percent; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Its capacity is no more than 80 percent of its prior capacity (in terms of bed size). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minimum payment level. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The minimum payment level for qualifying hospitals will be 70 percent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Limitation on the period for exception payments. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A qualifying hospital may receive an exceptions payment for up to 10 years from the year in which it first meets the age
of assets test, provided that it meets the age of asset test no later than the last cost reporting period beginning before
October 1, 2001. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determining a hospital's exception payment amount_
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cumulative comparison. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For each cost reporting period, the hospital's exception payment is determined by comparing the cumulative payments
made to the hospital under the capital prospective payment system to the cumulative minimum payment levels applicable
to the hospital for each cost reporting period subject to the prospective payment system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Offsetting amounts. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any amount by which the hospital's cumulative payments exceed its cumulative minimum payment levels is deducted
from the additional payment that would otherwise be payable for a cost reporting period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Other offset. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any amount by which the hospital's Medicare inpatient operating and capital prospective payments exceed its Medicare
inpatient operating and capital costs is deducted from the additional payment that would otherwise be payable for
the cost reporting period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Limit on exception payments. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Total estimated payments under the exception process may not exceed 10 percent of the total estimated capital prospective
payments (exclusive of hold-harmless payments for old capital) for the same fiscal year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

