<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
The chart shows that the cumulative effect of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
revised rates of increase is to lower the FY 1994 budget 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
neutrality target by 13.56 percent. Together with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
0.54 percent decline due to updated HCRIS data, this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accounts for the 14.01 percent reduction in the FY 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital cost per case budget neutrality target compared to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the level estimated at the time of the FY 1994 final rule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For FY 1994, we employed a budget neutrality factor of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
0.8947 to realize the 90 percent target. In this proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule for FY 1995, the budget neutrality adjustment factor is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
0.7986. The budget neutrality factors are not built 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanently into the rates; that is, the factors are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied cumulatively in determining the Federal rate. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
net adjustment to the FY 1994 Federal rate would therefore 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be .7986/.8947 or 0.8926. For the final rule, we will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recalculate the budget neutrality factor on the basis of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
most recent data available. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
5. Exceptions Payment Adjustment Factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Section 412.308(c)(3) requires that the standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal rate for inpatient capital-related costs be reduced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by an adjustment factor equal to the estimated additional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payments for exceptions under &sect;412.348 determined as a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proportion of total payments under the hospital-specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rate and Federal rate. The model developed for determining 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the budget neutrality adjustment factor is also used to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
estimate payments under the exceptions payment process and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to determine the exceptions payment adjustment factor. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For FY 1994, we estimated that exceptions payments 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would equal 5.15 percent of aggregate payments based on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal rate and the hospital-specific rate. Therefore, we 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied an exceptions reduction factor of 0.9485 (1^.0515) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in determining the Federal rate. For FY 1995, we estimate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that exceptions payments will equal 2.03 percent of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aggregate payments based on the Federal rate and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate. Therefore, we propose to apply an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exceptions reduction factor of 0.9797 (1^.0203) to determine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the FY 1995 Federal rate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The exceptions reductions factors are not built 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanently into the rates; that is, the factors are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied cumulatively in determining the Federal rate. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
net adjustment to the FY 1995 Federal rate is therefore 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
.9797/.9485, or 1.0329. The proposed exceptions reduction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor for FY 1995 is thus 3.29 percent higher than the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor for FY 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
6. Standard Federal Rate for FY 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
For FY 1994, the Federal rate was $378.34. With the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
changes we are proposing to the factors used to establish 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Federal rate, the FY 1995 Federal rate would be $353.87. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The proposed changes are as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The FY 1995 update factor would be 1.0222. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The FY 1995 outlier adjustment factor would be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
0.9372. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The FY 1995 budget neutrality adjustment factor that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is applied to the standard Federal payment rate for changes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the DRG relative weights and in the geographic adjustment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor would be 1.00115. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The FY 1995 budget neutrality adjustment factor that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is applied to the standard Federal payment rate and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate to assure that aggregate payments 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equal 90 percent of payments that would have been made on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable cost basis would be 0.7986. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The FY 1995 exceptions payments adjustment factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would be 0.9797. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Since the Federal rate has already been adjusted for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
differences in case mix, wages, cost of living, indirect 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
medical education costs, and payments to hospitals serving a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disproportionate share of low-income patients, we propose to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
make no additional adjustments in the standard Federal rate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for these factors other than the budget neutrality factors 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for changes in the DRG relative weights and the geographic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjustment factor. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
We are providing a chart that shows how each of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factors and adjustments for FY 1995 affected the computation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the proposed FY 1995 Federal rate in comparison to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1994 Federal rate. The FY 1995 update factor has the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
effect of increasing the Federal rate 2.22 percent compared 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the rate in FY 1994, while the geographic and DRG budget 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
neutrality factor has the effect of increasing the Federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rate by 0.12 percent. The FY 1995 exceptions reduction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor has the effect of increasing the Federal rate by 3.29 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percent compared to the exceptions reduction for FY 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The proposed FY 1995 budget neutrality adjustment factor has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the effect of reducing the final FY 1994 rate by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
10.74 percent compared to the budget neutrality reduction in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1994. The combined effect of all the proposed changes is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to decrease the proposed Federal rate by 6.47 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compared to the Federal rate for FY 1994.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

