We have refined our proposed budget neutrality and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exceptions reduction factors for FY 1995 on the basis of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
best available data. We have not retroactively adjusted the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal rate for FY 1994 in determining the rate for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
7. Special Rate for Puerto Rico Hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
For FY 1994, the special rate for Puerto Rico hospitals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
was $291.03. With the changes we are proposing to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factors used to determine the rate, we are proposing that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the FY 1995 special rate for Puerto Rico will be $272.20. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=4 -->
B. Determination of Hospital-Specific Rate Update 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Section 412.328(e) of the regulations provides that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate for FY 1995 be determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjusting the FY 1994 hospital-specific rate by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following factors: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
1. Hospital-Specific Rate Update Factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
The hospital-specific rate is updated in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the update factor for the standard Federal rate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined under &sect;412.308(c)(1). For FY 1995, we are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposing that the hospital-specific rate be updated by a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor of 1.0222. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
2. Exceptions Payment Adjustment Factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
For FY 1992 through FY 2001, the updated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate is multiplied by an adjustment factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equal to the estimated additional payments for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital-related costs for exceptions under &sect;412.348, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined as a proportion of the total amount of payments 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under the hospital-specific rate and the Federal rate. For 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FY 1995, we estimate that exceptions payments will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2.03 percent of aggregate payments based on the Federal rate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the hospital-specific rate. We therefore propose that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the updated hospital-specific rate be reduced by a factor of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
0.9797. The exceptions reductions factors are not built 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanently into the rates; that is, the factors are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied cumulatively in determining the hospital-specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rate. The net adjustment to the FY 1995 hospital-specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rate is therefore .9797/.9485, or 1.0329. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
3. Budget Neutrality Adjustment Factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
For FY 1992 through FY 1995, the updated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate is adjusted by a budget neutrality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjustment factor determined under &sect;412.352, so that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
estimated aggregate payments under the capital prospective 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment system will equal 90 percent of what would have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payable on a reasonable cost basis. (The budget neutrality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjustment for changes in the DRG relative weights and in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the geographic adjustment factor is not applied to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate.) For FY 1995, we are proposing a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
budget neutrality factor of 0.7986. The budget neutrality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor is not built permanently into the rates; that is, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factor is not applied cumulatively in determining the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate. The net adjustment to the FY 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate is therefore .7986/.8947, or 0.8926. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=4 -->
4. Net Change to Hospital-Specific Rate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
We are providing a chart below to show the proposed net 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
change to the hospital-specific rate. The chart shows the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
factors for FY 1994 and FY 1995 and the net adjustment for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each factor. It also shows that the proposed cumulative net 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjustment from FY 1994 to FY 1995 is 0.9424, which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
represents a decrease of 5.76 percent to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate. The proposed FY 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital-specific rate for each hospital is determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
multiplying the FY 1994 hospital-specific rate by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cumulative net adjustment of 0.9424.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

