<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</BILLING>

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0101 clearpage -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=2 -->
E. Projection of the CIPI for Fiscal Year 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
We project a 0.9 percent increase in the CIPI for FY 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1995 (Table 3 and Figure 6). This is the outcome of a 3.1 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percent increase in projected weighted depreciation prices 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in FY 1995 offset by a 3.6 percent decline in vintage- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
weighted interest rates in FY 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=2 -->
F. ProPAC Input Price Index 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=2 -->
1. Introduction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
Three major differences distinguish ProPAC's CIPI from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
HCFA's CIPI: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The ProPAC CIPI measures changes in capital asset 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purchase prices in the year the asset is purchased. HCFA's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
CIPI is designed to measure changes in a vintage-weighted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
composite of capital asset purchase prices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The ProPAC CIPI uses capital asset purchase price 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proxies that differ from HCFA's. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940527-1-00223 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940527-1-00014 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
&bull;The ProPAC CIPI has no interest component. PROPAC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
treats interest rate changes as a separate update factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
component. Through 1995, for example, ProPAC expects that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
long term interest rates will remain stable and, therefore, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
believes that it is not appropriate to adjust capital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payments for forecasted changes in interest rates in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
target year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
HCFA incorporates a vintage-weighted composite of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interest rates in its CIPI for the target year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 03 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

