<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0101 clearpage -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=2 -->
2. Depreciation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
ProPAC states that its CIPI is analogous to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prospective payment operating price index. We disagree. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The components of the operating index represent price 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
changes in ongoing hospital expenses for labor and non- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital goods and services. The analogous capital expenses 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in this context are current depreciation costs, interest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
costs and other capital-related expenses (taxes and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
insurance). Current depreciation and interest costs are a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cumulative composite of segments of expenses incurred in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
current and prior periods. Current interest costs are a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cumulative composite of segments of past and current year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
debt costs. Since both depreciation and interest costs have 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a vintage component, the price aspect of these costs must 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have a vintage component as well. The HCFA CIPI attempts to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capture these vintage components. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
