<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
We believe that the adjustment for capital efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and cost-effectiveness should take into account the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
efficiency and effectiveness of the capital resources 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
present in the base year for the capital prospective payment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system. We do not believe that Medicare capital payment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rates should provide for maintenance of capital in excess of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the level that would be produced in an efficiency-oriented 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
competitive market. The capital efficiency adjustment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
should be designed to give hospitals an incentive to reduce 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inefficiency and ineffectiveness in capital resources. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analysis in Table 4 suggests that, in order to restore the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal rate to the level at which it would have been if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital costs had not been excessive in the years before the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implementation of capital prospective payment, a cumulative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction in the rate of 28.2 percent (1.565/2.088=.7495, or -25.0 percent) is justified. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
We note that the Administration's Health Security Act 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contains a proposal for an annual adjustment to the capital 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
update for FY 1996 through FY 2003. This proposal is based 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in part on our previous analysis of capital spending in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years prior to the implementation of the capital prospective 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment system. Section 4103(a)(2)(C) of the proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Health Security Act provides that the annual update factor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied to the capital prospective payment system rates be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduced by 4.9 percent each year during that period (except 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that the change factor can never be negative in any year). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

